{"title":"2021 MPFG Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_MPFG_Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a regular tetrahedron. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> be the regular tetrahedron whose vertices are the centers of the faces of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumcenter of either tetrahedron. Given a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> different from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/8/06839317e8e060e9a63d404989b9ed7fdb05a494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m(P)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> be the midpoint of the points of intersection of the ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/26210ca120c90877ba6105fc77165ee47f386c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OP}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"22\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of eight points m(P) where P is a vertex of either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. What is the volume of the convex hull of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> divided by the volume of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />? Express your\nanswer as a fraction in simplest form.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_MPFG_Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Connect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with the 4 vertices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Extend the line made by connecting the top vertex of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, intersecting at the base/vertex of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> equals to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> regular tetrahedron with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> protruding tetrahedrons.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:New3d.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/25/New3d.png/600px-New3d.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"529\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/25/New3d.png/900px-New3d.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/25/New3d.png/1200px-New3d.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure> \n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2d.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/5f/2d.png/400px-2d.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"324\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/5f/2d.png/600px-2d.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/5f/2d.png/800px-2d.png 2x\" /></a></span> <span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Protrudes.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4c/Protrudes.png/500px-Protrudes.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"292\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4c/Protrudes.png/750px-Protrudes.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/4c/Protrudes.png/1000px-Protrudes.png 2x\" /></a></span> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d43952ff70c3a7873a6d649547993ab272e11d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{tetra} = (\\frac{5}{3})^3 = \\frac{125}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"158\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/0/0701e85278ad5bd6922f576051b560e191fb0aab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{total} = \\frac{125}{27} \\cdot (1+\\frac{\\frac{4}{3}}{\\frac{5}{3}}) = \\boxed{\\frac{25}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"228\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>~cassphe\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018063844\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 110/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4400/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:33575:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018063844 and revision id 266915. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}